00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
NHTSA data shows Tesla's Robotaxi fleet recorded just two minor low-speed scrapes in the latest reporting window. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 607. NHTSA ADS data covers the period from mid-July through August 17. Exactly two incidents appeared for the model y unsupervised fleet. Both involved contact below two miles per hour with stationary objects. No injuries occurred, and neither vehicle

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:37.240
needed a tow. A separate NHTSA order now requires Tesla to justify cybercab certification

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:43.560
under oath. The filing asks for sworn responses on specific certification questions. Those

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:48.080
two threads together put fresh pressure on the autonomy timeline and the regulatory

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:54.780
path forward. While autonomy faces both safety proof points and fresh questions, the semi-program

00:00:54.780 --> 00:01:00.840
is showing concrete manufacturing signals. Tesla is now deploying factory-built mega-chargers

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:06.940
that arrive pre-assembled. The same pre-fabricated approach sped up supercharger builds several years

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:14.260
ago. Tesla Roddy reports that the move signals preparation for higher semi-volumes, pre-assembled units

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:20.720
avoid on-site fabrication delays that previously slowed station construction. Energy infrastructure

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:25.240
progress leads naturally into Tesla's larger solar manufacturing ambitions.

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:32.980
Lamar consolidated ISD will vote on tax breaks for a proposed $10.1 billion solar plant in Fort Bend

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:38.680
County. The site sits near Needville, and the project would cover both cell and panel production.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:46.560
Discussions tie the facility to roughly 9,700 local jobs. Manufacturing scale in solar often

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:52.020
gets framed as a simple capacity race, yet the real constraint sits in how quickly new lines

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:57.560
can reach stable yield while meeting grid into connection timelines. Tesla's proposed

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:02.940
Fort Bend facility would add substantial domestic panel output, but the project's economics

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:08.160
depend on whether local incentives offset the higher upfront capital compared with existing

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:14.840
Asian supply chains. The vote by Lamar consolidated ISD on tax breaks will test how much local

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:19.640
governments are willing to trade for job numbers that may not materialize until the plant

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:21.800
reaches full utilization years later.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:28.420
The $10.1 billion investment figure includes both cell and panel manufacturing steps that

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:30.060
must be commissioned in sequence.

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:36.560
Vertical integration gives Tesla control over cell-to-panel assembly, yet it also concentrates

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:41.940
execution risk inside one company rather than spreading it across specialized suppliers.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:48.440
When a single line must deliver both volume and consistent quality, any delay in one process

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:50.980
step ripples through the entire cost curve.

